I’d like to talk about a university group project that I had to share with several other students. Our task was to develop an application and present it in front of our class.

I was assigned to work with three other students, and we had two months to complete the project. At first, it was quite difficult because we had different ideas and experiences, so we couldn't agree on what kind of application we should build. However, after discussing our ideas and compromising, we eventually came up with a concept that everyone was happy with.

I was responsible for researching similar products on the market and writing the product requirements. I had to make sure that our application included the most useful features. I was also in charge of developing some of the business logic and workflows. Another member worked on the user interface, while the others handled deployment and the presentation.

Throughout the project, we had to share our ideas, progress, and responsibilities with each other. We also had regular meetings to make sure everyone was on the same page. Sometimes, it was difficult to arrange meetings because we all had different schedules, but we learned to adapt and communicate effectively.

Eventually, we gave a presentation about our application in front of our lecturer and classmates. Fortunately, our lecturer was satisfied with the final result, and we received a lot of positive feedback. We even got a higher grade than we had expected.

Looking back, it was a great experience because it taught me the importance of cooperation, communication, and being willing to compromise. I believe these qualities will continue to benefit me in my future career.
